      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. PLATE loader: folder of your full-resolution source sequence.\n2. MATTE loader: folder of the coarse alpha (e.g. from LTX). Its mask output (channel red for a grey RGB matte) goes to 'matte'.\nUse the SAME first/last frame in both loaders so plate and matte stay in sync, and set the same number as start_frame in Save Matte Sequence.\n\n3. Tune core_erode / outer_dilate on the overlay preview until hair and motion blur lie inside the orange band.\n\nOptional: core_mask forces solid foreground, garbage_mask forces background (invert_garbage = roto drawn around the subject).\n\nLong 4K ranges need a lot of RAM (the loader prints an estimate). For very long shots use 'Pertineo ViTMatte Tiled (Sequence)' instead."
      ],
      "title": "How to use"
    },
